      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. but the parents who want the traditional approach say that focusing on the darker parts of history too much early on just makes kids feel guilty or divided instead of proud of their country. they also argue that kids at that age aren't emotionally ready for these heavy topics. wouldn't it be more effective to start with the shared values first to build a foundation of unity before getting into the more controversial stuff?",
